  "decision": "promising but not promoted: both retention settings were positive on every measured window, and the selected retention-8 candidate repeated a +2 net-map gain on a fresh 256-game confirmation, but the combined matched-map sign test remained non-significant at p=0.263",
  "conclusion": "Exposing root action Q-values made it possible to distinguish a search correction from a simple visit target and compressed a small repeatable fraction of the ranking-PUCT signal into a zero-search policy. The selected candidate improved 13 maps and regressed 7 across 384 development-plus-confirmation games, worth +23.99 arena-specific baseline-adjusted Elo, but the sparse discordant sample does not justify a release artifact. The implementation is retained for larger counterfactual datasets; the candidate is rejected from the model registry."
